+## Expansion: Surahs 18, 23, 32, 36 and 55
+
+The second expansion adds Al-Kahf, Al-Mu'minun, As-Sajdah, Ya-Sin and Ar-Rahman: 419 ayahs and 4,077 word occurrences, bringing the edition to 16 Surahs, 474 ayahs and 4,307 words. The chapters use the same `StudyData` shape, field meanings and validation as the existing lessons.
+
+**AI involvement is explicit:** the Arabic text is the Quran.com Uthmani text retrieved from the Content API, not generated; recitation signs that the API separates from a word by a space (waqf, saktah and sajdah signs and the rub al-hizb marker) are excluded from word tokens, following the Surahs 110–114 precedent, and every exclusion is listed in the inventory. Word types and roots are derived deterministically from Quranic Arabic Corpus 0.4 stem tags with the mapping that reproduces all 230 roots of the existing lessons. The Corpus file was used locally from a verbatim distribution checked by SHA-256 and is not bundled. Its word and verse i‘rab pages informed the syntax. Where a Corpus tag contradicts the vocalised word or its governing context (for example a passive or indicative verb tagged otherwise), the lesson follows the corrected analysis and the source audit lists each correction.
+
+Urdu meanings, translations, morphology/syntax/dictionary notes, phrase notes, verb-paradigm notes, root notes, rules and concise tafsir summaries are AI-assisted original teaching drafts. They were written by agents with Tafsir al-Muyassar, Tafsir al-Sa‘di and the abridged Ibn Kathir as references, and Saheeh International and Mufti Taqi Usmani translations as meaning checks. Each chunk of ayahs was then checked by two independent reviewers (grammar; meaning, tafsir and Urdu), corrected, and re-checked by a confirming reviewer. Verb paradigms and root entries come from shared libraries that were reviewed the same way. This is AI review and automated validation, **not scholarly approval**.
